# Recovering the run imposes |x-y| <= rho. Both scores obey current bounds.
# An integral min-cost flow maximizes sum a*(x-y) with both daily sums fixed.
# After subtracting each run's lower bound, X->i carries x and i->Y carries y;
# i<->Z carries x-y, with capacity rho in each direction.
def pair_width(B,data):
